<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:h="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" version="1.0" name="Context" initial="idle"><metadata><h:section id="documentation"><h:h2>Context — actor contract</h:h2><h:p><h:strong>Actor invariant: </h:strong>All prompt context is pinned by immutable manifest digest; evidence cannot override owner policy; active revision changes only future model calls.</h:p><h:p><h:strong>Specification: </h:strong>ACT-CONTEXT in <h:a href="../system.xml">system.xml</h:a>. These comments use XHTML namespace h: and are not executable SCXML actions.</h:p><h:h3>I/O contracts invoked by this actor</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CONTEXT-READ">review.context.read</h:a> — ContextGetRequest → ContextGetResult | Fault; read, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-039, FL-040, FL-035; requirements: REQ-077, REQ-080, REQ-088</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CONTEXT-BIND">review.context.bind</h:a> — ContextBindRequest → ContextBindResult | Fault; external-write, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-039; requirements: REQ-077, REQ-078</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-PERSONA-SAVE">review.context.savePersona</h:a> — PersonaSaveRequest → PersonaSaveResult | Fault; external-write, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-038; requirements: REQ-076, REQ-088</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CONTEXT-ADD">review.context.attachEvidence</h:a> — ContextSourceRequest → ContextSourceResult | Fault; external-write, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-040; requirements: REQ-079, REQ-088</h:li></h:ul></h:section></metadata><state id="idle">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-idle"><h:h3>State: idle</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>context.load</h:code> → loading</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="context.load" target="loading"/>
  </state>
  <state id="loading">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-loading"><h:h3>State: loading</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>context.ready</h:code> → ready<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CONTEXT-READ"> [typed result: IO-CONTEXT-READ]</h:a></h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="context.ready" target="ready"/>
  </state>
  <state id="ready">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-ready"><h:h3>State: ready</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>context.update</h:code> → updating</h:li><h:li><h:code>context.load</h:code> → loading</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="context.update" target="updating"/>
    <transition event="context.load" target="loading"/>
  </state>
  <state id="updating">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-updating"><h:h3>State: updating</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>context.saved</h:code> → ready<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CONTEXT-BIND"> [typed result: IO-CONTEXT-BIND]</h:a><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-PERSONA-SAVE"> [typed result: IO-PERSONA-SAVE]</h:a><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CONTEXT-ADD"> [typed result: IO-CONTEXT-ADD]</h:a></h:li><h:li><h:code>context.conflict</h:code> → conflict</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="context.saved" target="ready"/>
    <transition event="context.conflict" target="conflict"/>
  </state>
  <state id="conflict">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-conflict"><h:h3>State: conflict</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>context.load</h:code> → loading</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="context.load" target="loading"/>
  </state>
</scxml>
